{% import "macros/icons.njk" as ic %}

{% set heroPhoto = "secondary-students-classroom" %}
{% set heroShape = "tall" %}
{% set heroEyebrow = "Lower Secondary · Years 7 to 9 · ages 11 to 14" %}
{% set heroTitle = 'More independence, bigger <span class="mark">projects</span>' %}
{% set heroText = "Cambridge English, Maths and Science every morning, each with a specialist teacher. Classes of " + site.classCap + " or fewer, and students do more of the planning." %}
{% include "partials/pagehero.njk" %}

<section>
  <div class="wrap two">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--blue">The academic core</p>
      <h2>Subject teachers, real practical work</h2>
      <p>Each core subject has a teacher with a degree in it. <strong>English</strong> moves into literature and argument. <strong>Maths</strong> builds toward IGCSE. <strong>Science</strong> covers biology, chemistry and physics, with practical work every week.</p>
      <p>Students also take <strong>History</strong> and <strong>Executive Function</strong>: learning to plan, organise and finish things.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="leaf-wrap leaf-wrap--r has-sticker">
      <span class="sticker sticker--blue sticker--tr">Cambridge Lower Secondary</span>
      {% photo "secondary-marble-run-wall", "photo--lg photo--tilt-r" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% set waveColor = "pale" %}{% include "partials/wave.njk" %}
<section class="band--pale" id="day">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--blue">Monday to Friday</p>
      <h2>A Lower Secondary day</h2>
      <p class="lede">The core subjects first, then History or Executive Function. Afternoons are for making, moving and experiments.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt">{% set dayKey = "lower-secondary" %}{% include "partials/dayline.njk" %}</div>
  </div>
</section>
{% set waveColor = "white" %}{% include "partials/wave.njk" %}

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Beyond the core</p>
      <h2>Where it gets built</h2>
      <p class="lede">Specialist and vocational classes, in English, with the tools out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cards cards--3 mt">
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("flask", "blue") }}<h3>Art of Science</h3><p>Experiments that use the morning's science.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("tools", "green") }}<h3>Maker Space</h3><p>Technology and design. Tools, materials and a problem: students design, build, test and present.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("ball", "blue") }}<h3>Movement</h3><p>Sport and fitness.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("heart", "green") }}<h3>Wellbeing</h3><p>A class on the things that make the rest of the week go better.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("clock", "blue") }}<h3>Review</h3><p>Time to catch up and ask the question you did not ask in class.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("book", "green") }}<h3>History and Executive Function</h3><p>Late morning, before lunch. The past, and the habits that get work done: planning, organising, finishing.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="center mt"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ '/families/schedule/#lower-secondary' | url }}">See the week at a glance</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

{% set waveColor = "pale" %}{% include "partials/wave.njk" %}
<section class="band--pale">
  <div class="wrap two two--flip">
    <div class="leaf-wrap leaf-wrap--tint">
      {% photo "secondary-table-tennis", "photo--lg photo--tilt" %}
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">What comes next</p>
      <h2>Upper Secondary</h2>
      <p>After Lower Secondary, students move into <a href="{{ '/learning/upper-secondary/' | url }}">Upper Secondary</a>, with a US diploma or Cambridge pathway at their own pace.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% set waveColor = "white" %}{% include "partials/wave.njk" %}

<section class="faq">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Questions parents ask</h2>
    <details><summary>Can a student join partway through the year?</summary><p>Yes, we admit students all year. Tuition runs from your child's first day, and we meet them before they start so they join the right class.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do you handle gaps from a previous school?</summary><p>We meet every student and read their last report before they join, so we know where the gaps are. If we can meet your child's needs, we make a support plan with you; our teachers are trained to support autism, ADHD and learning differences. When a child needs more, we refer families to The LA Center for one-to-one support and assessments, arranged and paid for by the family.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do you teach Vietnamese?</summary><p>We offer Vietnamese as a second language. The language classes change from year to year with student interest and staffing, so ask us what is running this year.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

